# function scan(text, turns) { .. for (let turn = 0; turn < turns; turn = turn + 1) sum = sum + text.charCodeAt(turn); .. }
# A joined text is made flat in front of the loop that reads its characters. Where the loop runs no turn that is work and memory of the size of the text for nothing,
# so the head's own question is asked in front for the values that enter, and the flattening takes the answer: under a no it gives the empty text, which no turn reads.
# RUN: walk f1:Body mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: [[begins]]: boolean @Boolean = Less
# CHECK: = FlattenString {{*}}, [[begins]] traits
# CHECK: isLoopHead=true
# CHECK-NOT: = FlattenString
# function always(text, last) { .. do { sum = sum + text.charCodeAt(turn); before = turn; turn = turn + 1; } while (before < last); .. }: the reader stands in front of the question, so the first turn reads whatever the question says of what enters: nothing is asked
# RUN(ALWAYS): walk f2:Body mechanisms=all
# ALWAYS-LABEL: code f2:Body
# ALWAYS-NOT: = FlattenString {{*}}, v
# function once(text, turns) { .. sum = sum + text.charCodeAt(1) + turn; .. }: a unit that no turn changes is read in front of the typed copy, behind the yes of that question; its no leads to the closed copy
# RUN(ONCE): walk f3:Body mechanisms=all
# ONCE-LABEL: code f3:Body
# ONCE: isLoopHead=true
# ONCE: = GetStringCodeUnit
# ONCE: [[begins]]: boolean @Boolean = Less {{*}}form=Numbers
# ONCE: Branch [[begins]] -> taken [[front]](), notTaken
# ONCE: isLoopHead=true
# ONCE-NOT: = GetStringCodeUnit
# ONCE: [[front]]():
# ONCE: = GetStringCodeUnit
# layout L909 kind=Closure
